menu "I2S bring-up"

    config BRINGUP_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ
        int "I2S sample rate (Hz)"
        range 8000 48000
        default 16000
        help
            Sample rate for both the mic and the speaker. Issue #52 asks to try 8000
            to see whether the mic still gives sensible readings at that rate.

    config BRINGUP_NOISE_FLOOR_DBFS
        int "Quiet-room noise floor (dBFS)"
        range -120 0
        default -80
        help
            The mic level measured in a quiet room. -80 is a placeholder until it is
            measured on the real board. The meter prints how far each reading is
            above this value, so a clap shows up as a big positive number.

    config BRINGUP_TONE_ENABLE
        bool "Play a test tone on the speaker"
        default y

    config BRINGUP_TONE_CYCLE
        bool "Cycle through the issue #52 test tones"
        depends on BRINGUP_TONE_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            Steps through silence, 60, 120, 180 and 440 Hz, a few seconds each, and
            labels every mic reading with the tone that was playing. One run gives
            all the Step 5 measurements. Turn this off to play one fixed tone instead.

    config BRINGUP_TONE_STEP_SECONDS
        int "Seconds per tone when cycling"
        depends on BRINGUP_TONE_CYCLE
        range 1 60
        default 5

    config BRINGUP_TONE_FREQ_HZ
        int "Fixed tone frequency (Hz)"
        depends on BRINGUP_TONE_ENABLE && !BRINGUP_TONE_CYCLE
        range 20 4000
        default 440

    config BRINGUP_TONE_AMPLITUDE_PCT
        int "Tone amplitude (% of full scale)"
        depends on BRINGUP_TONE_ENABLE
        range 1 50
        default 10
        help
            Keep this low at first. 10% is about -20 dBFS.

endmenu
